{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-93739",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Let's check each pair in turn.\n\n- $(1,4)$ is a solution of our equation. Indeed, substituting $x=1$ and $y=4,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9x-2y & =1 \\\\ 9\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 4 & =1 \\\\ 9-8 & =1 \\\\ 1 & =1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $(10,45)$ is *not* a solution of our equation. Substituting $x=10$ and $y=45,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9x-2y & =1 \\\\ 9\\cdot 10-2\\cdot 45 & =1 \\\\ 90-90 & =1 \\\\ 0 & \\ne 1\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $(5,22)$ is a solution of our equation. Indeed, substituting $x=5$ and $y=22,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9x-2y & =1 \\\\ 9\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 22 & =1 \\\\ 45-44 & =1 \\\\ 1 & =1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
